<div class="column-control push-bottom-small aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">

















    <div class="column-control__container
            
             grid
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
            ">

        
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-mobile ">





    
    
    <div class="accordion parbase">

     
     
     
     <div class="cmp-accordion one-column standard " data-initially-expanded-item="0">


<div class="aem-Grid aem-Grid--12 aem-Grid--default--12 ">
    
    <div class="accordion-item parbase aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">



    
    
    <div class="cmp-accordion-item">
        <div class="cmp-accordion-item__container">
            <div class="cmp-accordion-item__text">
                <div class="cmp-accordion-item__header" role="heading" aria-expanded="true">
                    <div class="title">How do I determine which protection device is right for my application?</div>
                    
    <span class="cmp-accordion-item__icon-expand raw-file-contents" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M24.486 12.447l-8.88 5.474-8.063-5.456a.8.8 0 1 0-.897 1.325l8.491 5.745c.261.176.6.184.868.018l9.32-5.745a.8.8 0 1 0-.839-1.36z"/></svg>
    </span>

                </div>
                <div class="cmp-accordion-item__content" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div>


<div class="aem-Grid aem-Grid--12 aem-Grid--default--12 ">
    
    <div class="text aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">

<div class="cmp-text">
    <p>Choosing the appropriate protection device depends on factors such as system voltage, load type, available fault current and coordination needs. The portfolio includes options for motor protection, branch circuit protection and equipment isolation. Reviewing system drawings and using product selection tools can help narrow down suitable choices.</p>

</div>

    

</div>

    
</div>
</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cmp-accordion-item__image ">
                






    
    
        
        
        

        

        

        
        

        
    


            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
<div class="accordion-item parbase aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">



    
    
    <div class="cmp-accordion-item">
        <div class="cmp-accordion-item__container">
            <div class="cmp-accordion-item__text">
                <div class="cmp-accordion-item__header" role="heading" aria-expanded="true">
                    <div class="title">What benefits do coordinated protection solutions provide?</div>
                    
    <span class="cmp-accordion-item__icon-expand raw-file-contents" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M24.486 12.447l-8.88 5.474-8.063-5.456a.8.8 0 1 0-.897 1.325l8.491 5.745c.261.176.6.184.868.018l9.32-5.745a.8.8 0 1 0-.839-1.36z"/></svg>
    </span>

                </div>
                <div class="cmp-accordion-item__content" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div>


<div class="aem-Grid aem-Grid--12 aem-Grid--default--12 ">
    
    <div class="text aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">

<div class="cmp-text">
    <p>Coordinated protection solutions are designed so that the device closest to a fault responds first, helping limit unnecessary system interruptions and avoiding broader power loss. This approach supports overall system reliability, maintenance efficiency and clear fault isolation. Allen‑Bradley devices are designed to work cohesively, which can streamline engineering and simplify troubleshooting. Additional details are available on the Circuit Breakers and Motor Protection product pages.</p>

</div>

    

</div>

    
</div>
</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cmp-accordion-item__image ">
                






    
    
        
        
        

        

        

        
        

        
    


            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
<div class="accordion-item parbase aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">



    
    
    <div class="cmp-accordion-item">
        <div class="cmp-accordion-item__container">
            <div class="cmp-accordion-item__text">
                <div class="cmp-accordion-item__header" role="heading" aria-expanded="true">
                    <div class="title">When should I use a disconnect switch instead of a breaker?</div>
                    
    <span class="cmp-accordion-item__icon-expand raw-file-contents" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M24.486 12.447l-8.88 5.474-8.063-5.456a.8.8 0 1 0-.897 1.325l8.491 5.745c.261.176.6.184.868.018l9.32-5.745a.8.8 0 1 0-.839-1.36z"/></svg>
    </span>

                </div>
                <div class="cmp-accordion-item__content" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div>


<div class="aem-Grid aem-Grid--12 aem-Grid--default--12 ">
    
    <div class="text aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">

<div class="cmp-text">
    <p>Disconnect switches are commonly used for lockout/tagout procedures and for establishing isolation before equipment maintenance. Circuit breakers provide overcurrent protection but may not meet isolation requirements in all jurisdictions. Many systems use both devices together to meet safety and operational needs. Standards‑specific details are available on the Disconnect Switches product page.</p>

</div>

    

</div>

    
</div>
</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cmp-accordion-item__image ">
                






    
    
        
        
        

        

        

        
        

        
    


            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
<div class="accordion-item parbase aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">



    
    
    <div class="cmp-accordion-item">
        <div class="cmp-accordion-item__container">
            <div class="cmp-accordion-item__text">
                <div class="cmp-accordion-item__header" role="heading" aria-expanded="true">
                    <div class="title">How do low-voltage motor protectors improve system uptime?</div>
                    
    <span class="cmp-accordion-item__icon-expand raw-file-contents" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M24.486 12.447l-8.88 5.474-8.063-5.456a.8.8 0 1 0-.897 1.325l8.491 5.745c.261.176.6.184.868.018l9.32-5.745a.8.8 0 1 0-.839-1.36z"/></svg>
    </span>

                </div>
                <div class="cmp-accordion-item__content" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div>


<div class="aem-Grid aem-Grid--12 aem-Grid--default--12 ">
    
    <div class="text aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">

<div class="cmp-text">
    <p style="text-align: left;">Low‑voltage motor protectors monitor conditions such as overloads, phase imbalance and excessive heating. By detecting issues early and responding appropriately, they support motor protection and can help limit unplanned interruptions. Integrated diagnostics can assist maintenance teams in identifying root causes before equipment is restarted.</p>

</div>

    

</div>

    
</div>
</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cmp-accordion-item__image ">
                






    
    
        
        
        

        

        

        
        

        
    


            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
<div class="accordion-item parbase aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">



    
    
    <div class="cmp-accordion-item">
        <div class="cmp-accordion-item__container">
            <div class="cmp-accordion-item__text">
                <div class="cmp-accordion-item__header" role="heading" aria-expanded="true">
                    <div class="title">Are these products compatible with my existing Rockwell Automation control system?</div>
                    
    <span class="cmp-accordion-item__icon-expand raw-file-contents" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M24.486 12.447l-8.88 5.474-8.063-5.456a.8.8 0 1 0-.897 1.325l8.491 5.745c.261.176.6.184.868.018l9.32-5.745a.8.8 0 1 0-.839-1.36z"/></svg>
    </span>

                </div>
                <div class="cmp-accordion-item__content" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div>


<div class="aem-Grid aem-Grid--12 aem-Grid--default--12 ">
    
    <div class="text aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">

<div class="cmp-text">
    <p>Allen‑Bradley protection devices are designed for compatibility across motor control centers, drives, overload relays and industrial control panels. They support standard wiring practices and, where available, digital add‑ons that integrate into existing automation architectures.</p>

</div>

    

</div>

    
</div>
</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cmp-accordion-item__image ">
                






    
    
        
        
        

        

        

        
        

        
    


            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>

    
</div>
</div>

</div>



